module bindings.php.twig_string_template_unsandboxed_render;

// Twig's documented boundary for a template whose source the program did
// not write is the sandbox: the security chapter of Twig's own
// documentation requires the sandbox extension whenever template authors
// are untrusted. `Environment::createTemplate($source)` compiles markup
// handed to it at runtime -- the string form of `load()`, with no loader
// and no path involved -- so rendering a template built that way executes
// whatever the string contains, and only the environment's policy bounds
// what it can reach. Compiling a string and rendering it with no sandbox
// vocabulary anywhere in the file is the same incomplete template
// validation already reported for an environment on a loader of the
// application's own, a sandbox policy driven by blocked names, and a
// Smarty policy that inverts its allow-list.
//
// The shape is read at module scope because the sandbox is a property of
// the environment, and the common layout configures the environment where
// it is built -- a factory, a container getter, an init method -- rather
// than at the render site, so requiring the policy in the rendering
// function alone would report a renderer whose environment is in fact
// sandboxed. `createTemplate` is also Smarty's name for loading a
// template by resource name, which compiles nothing the caller handed it,
// so the clauses are confined to files that name Twig. Any spelling of
// the sandbox clears the issue (`Twig\Sandbox`, `SandboxExtension`, the
// enable/disable helpers on it); every clause is text-level over the
// module context, so a comment naming the sandbox clears too:
// false-negative direction only.
binding twigStringTemplateUnsandboxedRender {
  query pattern presenceNode where node.scope == "module" and node.context.language == "php" and containsAny(node.token, ["->createTemplate("]) and containsAny(node.token, ["->render("]) and containsAny(node.token, ["Twig", "twig"]) and not containsAny(node.token, ["Sandbox"])
  emit issue code.IncompleteTemplateValidation at node
}
